/-!
# KFB: the `phase` step as a fine-cost item-language program

The state `x : Fin W × Addr m (Fin n) → ℂ` of the restricted interface is encoded role-major
as a Gaussian array: role `w`, address `b` at index `w · 2^{mn} + aidx b`, where
`aidx b = Σ_{(r,c)} b(r,c) · 2^{c + n r}` (`finProdFinEquiv`).

`phaseP` = one scalar pass `i^{k₀ + k₁ n}` and one diagonal pass per address bit `(r, c)`
(multiplying by `i^{a_r}` where the bit is set), each a `qopW` on the segment of role `w`.

* `segApply` / `getD_segApply`: index semantics of one segment pass.
* `rep_phase`: if `zs` encodes `x`, the result encodes `(RStep.den T (phase w k₀ k₁ a)) *ᵥ x`.
* `phaseP_fsp`: the program, its result and its fine cost
  `(mn + 1) · O((W + 1) 2^{mn} (w + 1))`.
-/

